1
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:09,960
Imagine waking up tomorrow morning...

2
00:00:10,230 --> 00:00:14,400
...and discovering that you are the only person left on Earth.

3
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:15,900
No messages.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,280
No phone calls.

5
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:18,340
No traffic.

6
00:00:18,570 --> 00:00:21,430
No voices coming from the apartment next door.

7
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:26,050
At first, you might think something unusual happened overnight.

8
00:00:26,390 --> 00:00:27,730
Maybe it's a holiday.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,730
Maybe there's a power outage.

10
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:32,730
Maybe everyone is simply somewhere else.

11
00:00:33,210 --> 00:00:35,750
But then... you look outside.

12
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,950
And you realize something is terribly wrong.

13
00:00:39,450 --> 00:00:41,120
Every street is empty.

14
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:43,070
Every building is silent.

15
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:46,010
And somewhere between yesterday and today...

16
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:48,380
...humanity disappeared.

17
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:51,580
This is the story of Noah.

18
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:57,450
And this is what could happen... if you were the last human on Earth.
